{
    "word": "buzzsaw",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "1dba2fdd-17a0-3ce9-a62b-302750f31f1e",
                "word": "buzzsaw",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c5a08761-f31b-4f30-933a-61d1250f5d55",
                        "entry_id": "1dba2fdd-17a0-3ce9-a62b-302750f31f1e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "buzzsaws"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3b941bca-f47d-30d4-aa24-f2a1e0a14ee8",
                        "entry_id": "1dba2fdd-17a0-3ce9-a62b-302750f31f1e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A circular saw."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d3852432-8b87-4d3a-8c88-ba5edd380f2f",
                                "sense_id": "3b941bca-f47d-30d4-aa24-f2a1e0a14ee8",
                                "text": "Agriculture Secretary Edward T. Schafer is preparing to walk into a buzzsaw of criticism over American biofuels policy when he meets with world leaders to discuss the global food crisis next week."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "63d47c32-136f-37ef-aaf1-aa1b94302046",
                        "entry_id": "1dba2fdd-17a0-3ce9-a62b-302750f31f1e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone or something that makes a loud, harsh, grinding or rasping noise, like that of a circular saw."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0aa23f8f-da31-4645-b7a6-dc5f85f5291b",
                                "sense_id": "63d47c32-136f-37ef-aaf1-aa1b94302046",
                                "text": "No danger of these buzzsaws waking up, it was enough to make you wish for impaired hearing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "61eb7616-5841-42ad-b7ef-276ed0c64cac",
                                "sense_id": "63d47c32-136f-37ef-aaf1-aa1b94302046",
                                "text": "Anyway, buzzsaw hardcore from both bands with nice 'n' trebly production, and each have some Japanese influences in there."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "92c37901-d2b1-441b-a92e-f61ec20f6dab",
                                "sense_id": "63d47c32-136f-37ef-aaf1-aa1b94302046",
                                "text": "Nasal buzzsaws shook the sides of the tent as finally, they were all out for night."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ae07dd7-f1ce-45c6-b185-03acf171b38e",
                                "sense_id": "63d47c32-136f-37ef-aaf1-aa1b94302046",
                                "text": "In the darkness, Benny listened to the sounds of the street: a far-off police siren, a dog's growl, a hip-hop pulse blaring from a car stereo, the buzzsaw whine of the El."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0dcbe547-d172-3aaa-8c8a-13cdd2ec9740",
                        "entry_id": "1dba2fdd-17a0-3ce9-a62b-302750f31f1e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The MG 42 general-purpose machine gun."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b4042426-d410-49ef-99c5-771fbf7dcb3e",
                                "sense_id": "0dcbe547-d172-3aaa-8c8a-13cdd2ec9740",
                                "text": "Golden tracers from the jaggering MG42 buzzsaw lit up the air like glitter, and from both directions there were bee-hive-volumes of whizzes and snaps as bullets passed through the air, in some cases only feet from them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0eac0618-5128-439f-914d-a3a2dc1b338c",
                                "sense_id": "0dcbe547-d172-3aaa-8c8a-13cdd2ec9740",
                                "text": "Suddenly, machine-gun rounds tore over their heads, stitching a neat row of holes in the wall above them, the weapon's unmistakable ripping report identifying it as a 'buzz saw', as the GIs had nicknamed the German MG42 because of its stupendous rate of fire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef35ce0b-02ec-4cce-a988-2290827e45dd",
                                "sense_id": "0dcbe547-d172-3aaa-8c8a-13cdd2ec9740",
                                "text": "Cade braced its stock against his shoulder, sighted the moving shadows in the woods, and let the buzz saw chew into them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5825ce1a-7889-48b8-8eb3-3a33cc207297",
                                "sense_id": "0dcbe547-d172-3aaa-8c8a-13cdd2ec9740",
                                "text": "On Omaha Beach, the Panzer Army locked up the beachhead with eight concrete bunkers, with their buzzsaw MG-42 machine guns that fired 1,500 rounds per minute, aimed from 35 pillboxes with automatic artillery pieces of different sizes."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3f2ffa1d-9966-3b1d-a564-fbe61c0214b5",
                        "entry_id": "1dba2fdd-17a0-3ce9-a62b-302750f31f1e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A violently destructive attack."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "031eab95-a247-4734-9998-46a332b1f2b7",
                                "sense_id": "3f2ffa1d-9966-3b1d-a564-fbe61c0214b5",
                                "text": "The changes ran into a buzzsaw of Congressional criticism."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "36375b2b-9df6-4c1e-83a1-a50d957973fb",
                                "sense_id": "3f2ffa1d-9966-3b1d-a564-fbe61c0214b5",
                                "text": "Downsizings attack managers like an emotional buzzsaw."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "64ec4ced-690d-4cb9-b53d-820f70f7a2b8",
                                "sense_id": "3f2ffa1d-9966-3b1d-a564-fbe61c0214b5",
                                "text": "Landry's martyrdom was automatic and mostly unavoidable -- although Jerry, bless his heart, went into his initial press conference at Valley Ranch and walked right into his second media buzzsaw."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "891aec23-1ae8-48d4-bc84-4151259461e9",
                                "sense_id": "3f2ffa1d-9966-3b1d-a564-fbe61c0214b5",
                                "text": "But aware of it or not, Johnson was heading into a buzzsaw."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d12e1c8-5223-4851-bbe0-0857e7745fe1",
                                "sense_id": "3f2ffa1d-9966-3b1d-a564-fbe61c0214b5",
                                "text": "We knew that we were headed into a buzzsaw and some of us might not come back, a thought so absurd and so real that it was overwhelming."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "21f2fa53-30f3-4873-acfd-e8a36cd01541",
                                "sense_id": "3f2ffa1d-9966-3b1d-a564-fbe61c0214b5",
                                "text": "The old wood and plasterboard vaporized under the buzzsaw of .30 caliber bullets."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "96ed01b9-76aa-3f19-a59f-49898df95251",
                        "entry_id": "1dba2fdd-17a0-3ce9-a62b-302750f31f1e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who attacks violently and/or mindlessly."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4cca5610-33e3-4d7d-9e05-64713bca53f5",
                                "sense_id": "96ed01b9-76aa-3f19-a59f-49898df95251",
                                "text": "So he keeps away from the intellectual buzzsaws; and, as both philology and philosophy grow ever more and more technical, the gap between them, if anything, widens."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "30771912-89b9-41aa-a317-7877e77c0064",
                                "sense_id": "96ed01b9-76aa-3f19-a59f-49898df95251",
                                "text": "Apparently the jay was unaware that the hawk no longer had its hold because it became a buzzsaw of blue fury, slashing the hawk several more times."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c531629-7c3c-4dd9-89ee-95f72f1a2c29",
                                "sense_id": "96ed01b9-76aa-3f19-a59f-49898df95251",
                                "text": "Similarly , if mom or dad choose to do something other than play with the little feathered buzzsaws, as occasionally we humans do , the birds would have no choice but to \"play\" with whatever was handy: chairs, lamps, cabinets, pillows, or original Picasso... you get the idea."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd698b90-f0bc-4177-9a44-675bcad7f782",
                                "sense_id": "96ed01b9-76aa-3f19-a59f-49898df95251",
                                "text": "But the minute he arrived, he ran into a buzzsaw named Lee Iacocca."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c2b5744-9546-4d7c-9200-c540aaf8c7cd",
                                "sense_id": "96ed01b9-76aa-3f19-a59f-49898df95251",
                                "text": "Perhaps it's habit, an ingrained autonomous component to feeding, a lingering artifact from when they were still alive, thinking creatures instead of walking buzzsaws."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
